{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Closed the chunk retry question. The chunk writer does not resend individual chunks: a chunk the sink does not accept marks the writer failed with ErrSnapshotStreaming, and node.stream classifies that as a stream abort and returns nil, so the whole snapshot is retried later through the replicate path; on the receiving side gc removes the temp directory and drops the tracked slot once the chunk timeout elapses. Marked the investigation explained with defect_claim refuted, answered the gap as resolved, and kept the partial-data retention until timeout and the unmeasured retry cadence as limits. Source reasoning only.\"}"}}
